## `REVIEW-STATE.md`

```md
# Review State: <scope title>

## Status

- Scope: <caller-defined identifier, e.g. a feature slug or project name>
- Last Updated: <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ>

## Reviewed Files

| File Path | Status | Diff Fingerprint | Evidence Tier | Last Reviewed |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| <relative/path/to/file> | <passed \| needs_detailed_review \| stale> | <sha256-or-none> | <tier-1 \| tier-2 \| tier-3 \| tier-4 \| tier-5> | <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ> |

## Interpretation Notes

- `Status` values:
  - `passed`: reviewed and the stored `Diff Fingerprint` matches the file's current content.
  - `needs_detailed_review`: fingerprint mismatch detected, or the reviewer explicitly deferred a finding for deeper review; never silently trust this row as passed.
  - `stale`: file has changed since last review and no re-review has occurred yet.
- `Diff Fingerprint` is the hash `code-reviewer` itself uses to detect staleness (see the skill's "Review State" section) — a mismatch against the file's current content always downgrades `Status` to `needs_detailed_review`.
- `Evidence Tier` reflects the evidence-tier model defined in `skills/code-reviewer/SKILL.md`.
- One row per reviewed file; update the row in place on re-review rather than appending duplicate rows (append-only history belongs in `REVIEW-HISTORY.md`).
- When `code-reviewer` opens a review dashboard Artifact (see its "Visual Review" section), that Artifact is a live rendering of these exact rows plus the diff hunks — this table stays the durable source of truth either way.
```
